Facts about ESP32 chips and development boards (pin functions, strapping pins, header layouts, panic
formats) are taken from Espressif documentation (ESP-IDF, esp-dev-kits) and are cited per rule with URL
and retrieval date in data/sources/. No Espressif text is reproduced beyond short quotations used as
evidence.

Runtime dependencies (installed by Hermes, not bundled):
- schemdraw (MIT License)
- pyserial (BSD 3-Clause License)

External tools used through their command line only (installed by the user, not bundled, not imported):
- PlatformIO Core (Apache License 2.0)
- esptool (GPL-2.0-or-later)
- addr2line from GNU Binutils, as shipped in the Espressif toolchains (GPL-3.0-or-later)

Short quotations from third-party datasheets, application notes and safety guides are used as evidence
for individual rules and are cited with URL and retrieval date in data/sources/ (among others: NXP UM10204
I2C-bus specification, onsemi 2N2222A and 1N4001 datasheets, Nichicon and Rubycon capacitor documents,
Kingbright LED datasheet, Panasonic and Digi-Key battery safety guides, U.S. FDA laser FAQ). All rights
remain with their owners; no document is reproduced in full.

The module catalog (data/modules/) quotes single lines from the chip makers' datasheets as evidence for each
value, with page, URL, retrieval date and the SHA-256 of the cited file. The repository's tests/corpus/excerpts/
holds the same kind of short excerpts for the citation tests (not part of the installed plugin); one of them is from
Wikipedia and stays under CC BY-SA 4.0.
